about_32: text "Two ways to store a graph. An adjacency matrix has a cell for every pair of nodes; an adjacency list keeps each node's neighbours. Matrices suit dense graphs, lists sparse ones such as roads or social networks." @ 16,3897 192x13 [in=adjacency]

