note_4: text "Relax every edge, n − 1 times. B → A costs −3, so A drops from 4 to 2, and C to 4. If a pass still improves anything, there's a negative cycle." @ 206,4012 144x16 [in=bellman]
s -> a_7 : "4"
s -> b_6 : "5"
b_6 -> a_7 : "−3"
a_7 -> c_7 : "2"
b_6 -> c_7 : "6"
about_34: text "Bellman-Ford: shortest paths from one node, even when some edges are negative. Relax every edge n − 1 times; a pass that still improves something means a negative cycle. Used in network routing (distance vector)." @ 206,4034 144x17 [in=bellman]

